research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-f-cofinality.log-4691-research/audit/wave4-proof-contracts.json:24:    "fs-cardinal-exponentiation-is-strictly-monotone-in-the-base",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-f-cofinality.log-4692-research/audit/wave4-proof-contracts.json:3440:    "thm-cofinality-basics": {
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-f-cofinality.log-4693-research/audit/wave4-proof-contracts.json:3444:          "source": "def-cofinality",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-f-cofinality.log-4694-research/audit/wave4-proof-contracts.json:3446:          "quote": "Let $\\alpha$ be an ordinal ([[def-ordinal]]). The **cofinality** of $\\alpha$ is\n\n$$\\operatorname{cf}(\\alpha) \\;:=\\; \\text{the least ordinal } \\beta \\text{ for which some } f : \\beta \\to \\alpha \\text{ has cofinal range},$$\n\ncofinal range meaning that $f[\\beta]$ is a cofinal subset of $\\alpha$\n([[def-cofinal-subset-of-an-ordinal]]): every $\\zeta \\in \\alpha$ satisfies\n$\\zeta \\le f(\\xi)$ for some $\\xi \\in \\beta$. That such a least ordinal exists, and\nthat a witnessing map of that length may be taken strictly increasing, is\n[[lem-cofinality-is-well-defined]], and both are theorems of ZF. So\n$\\operatorname{cf}$ is defined at every ordinal, without any choice principle.\n\n**Regular and singular.** An **infinite cardinal** $\\kappa$\n([[def-cardinal]], [[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]]) is\n\n- **regular** when $\\operatorname{cf}(\\kappa) = \\kappa$;\n- **singular** when $\\operatorname{cf}(\\kappa) \\ne \\kappa$.\n\nThe two cases are exhaustive by definition, and by\n[[thm-cofinality-basics]] singular means exactly\n$\\operatorname{cf}(\\kappa) < \\kappa$, since $\\operatorname{cf}(\\alpha) \\le \\alpha$\nalways holds.",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-f-cofinality.log:4695:research/audit/wave4-proof-contracts.json:3756:        "notes": "Read in full by an independent read-only GPT 5.6 Sol proof-refuter lane (wave-4 lane `f4-cofinality`) at the DeepSeek/Sonnet judges' adversarial standard: every numbered step against its cited facts, every [F#]/[L#]/[A#] fact against the cited target opened on disk, the title and Statement against what the proof licenses, the declared choice cost against what the steps actually spend, and every Remark with a numbered step's suspicion. Alpha adjudicated each returned finding from disk under the binding 30-second threshold, recording confirmations, refutations and the repairs applied in research/audit/wave4-alpha.md. This item carries an A4 and/or A6 repair; its final text is certified by an independent Sol certifier lane (`f-cofinality`), which did not author it."
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-f-cofinality.log-4696-research/audit/wave4-proof-contracts.json:3759:    "thm-regularity-of-the-alephs": {
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-f-cofinality.log-4697-research/audit/wave4-proof-contracts.json:3763:          "source": "thm-cofinality-basics",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-f-cofinality.log-4698-research/audit/wave4-proof-contracts.json:3765:          "quote": "Work in ZF; no choice principle is used. Let $\\operatorname{cf}$ be the\ncofinality of [[def-cofinality]]. Then:\n\n**(a)** $\\operatorname{cf}(\\alpha) \\le \\alpha$ for every ordinal $\\alpha$\n([[def-ordinal]]);\n\n**(b)** $\\operatorname{cf}(0) = 0$, and $\\operatorname{cf}(\\alpha + 1) = 1$ for\nevery ordinal $\\alpha$, where $\\alpha + 1 = \\alpha \\cup \\{\\alpha\\}$\n([[def-ordinal-addition]]);\n\n**(c)** for a limit ordinal $\\lambda$ ([[def-limit-ordinal]]),\n$\\operatorname{cf}(\\lambda)$ is an **infinite cardinal** ([[def-cardinal]]) and\n$\\operatorname{cf}(\\operatorname{cf}(\\lambda)) = \\operatorname{cf}(\\lambda)$, so\n$\\operatorname{cf}(\\lambda)$ is a **regular** cardinal;\n\n**(d)** for a limit ordinal $\\lambda$, every cofinal $C \\subseteq \\lambda$\n([[def-cofinal-subset-of-an-ordinal]]) satisfies\n$\\operatorname{cf}(\\lambda) \\le \\lvert C \\rvert$, and some cofinal subset of\n$\\lambda$ has cardinality exactly $\\operatorname{cf}(\\lambda)$.\n\nClause (c) is what discharges the naming obligation of [[def-cofinality]]:\n\"regular\" is defined through $\\operatorname{cf}$, and it is a theorem, not a\nconvention, that $\\operatorname{cf}$ of a limit ordinal is a cardinal at which\nthe definition can be tested.",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-f-cofinality.log-4699-research/audit/wave4-proof-contracts.json:3774:          "source": "def-cofinality",
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/certifier-certify-f-cofinality.log-4700-research/audit/wave4-proof-contracts.json:3776:          "quote": "Let $\\alpha$ be an ordinal ([[def-ordinal]]). The **cofinality** of $\\alpha$ is\n\n$$\\operatorname{cf}(\\alpha) \\;:=\\; \\text{the least ordinal } \\beta \\text{ for which some } f : \\beta \\to \\alpha \\text{ has cofinal range},$$\n\ncofinal range meaning that $f[\\beta]$ is a cofinal subset of $\\alpha$\n([[def-cofinal-subset-of-an-ordinal]]): every $\\zeta \\in \\alpha$ satisfies\n$\\zeta \\le f(\\xi)$ for some $\\xi \\in \\beta$. That such a least ordinal exists, and\nthat a witnessing map of that length may be taken strictly increasing, is\n[[lem-cofinality-is-well-defined]], and both are theorems of ZF. So\n$\\operatorname{cf}$ is defined at every ordinal, without any choice principle.\n\n**Regular and singular.** An **infinite cardinal** $\\kappa$\n([[def-cardinal]], [[def-aleph-and-beth-hierarchies]]) is\n\n- **regular** when $\\operatorname{cf}(\\kappa) = \\kappa$;\n- **singular** when $\\operatorname{cf}(\\kappa) \\ne \\kappa$.\n\nThe two cases are exhaustive by definition, and by\n[[thm-cofinality-basics]] singular means exactly\n$\\operatorname{cf}(\\kappa) < \\kappa$, since $\\operatorname{cf}(\\alpha) \\le \\alpha$\nalways holds.",
