research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-separation-urysohn.log-308772-+> The order rays $(-\infty,\tfrac12)$ and $(\tfrac12,\infty)$ are open in the usual topology of $\mathbb R$ (`lem-real-line-is-a-metric-space`, clause 3), so their traces $[0,\tfrac12)$ and $(\tfrac12,1]$ are open in the subspace topology of $[0,1]$ (`def-subspace-topology-top`, `def-interval`). They are disjoint and contain $0$ and $1$, respectively.
