research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-7054-items/thm-compactness-variants-hierarchy.md:129:**Why claim 4 needs the singleton hypothesis and claim 1(c) does not.** A limit point of the set $A$ built at step 2.1 need not be one of the $x_n$ with large index unless the finitely many early terms can be cut away, and cutting them away is exactly what closedness of singletons permits. Without that hypothesis the implication fails, and the witness is worked on this page's companion, as `cex-limit-point-compact-without-countable-compactness`: a space in which every nonempty subset has a limit point, for the trivial reason that each point has a partner it cannot be separated from, and which has a countable open cover with no finite subcover.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-7055-items/thm-compactness-variants-hierarchy.md:130:
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-7056-items/thm-compactness-variants-hierarchy.md:131:**None of the reverse implications holds in general.** Compactness is strictly stronger than countable compactness ([[fs-countably-compact-implies-compact]]), sequential compactness neither implies nor is implied by compactness ([[fs-compact-implies-sequentially-compact]], [[fs-sequentially-compact-implies-compact]]), and each of those false statements carries a witness reachable from this page.
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-7057-items/thm-compactness-variants-hierarchy.md:132:
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log:7058:items/thm-compactness-variants-hierarchy.md:133:**For a metrizable space the picture collapses.** Compactness, countable compactness, sequential compactness and limit point compactness are all equivalent there ([[thm-metric-compactness-equivalences]]), at a choice cost recorded arrow by arrow in [[rem-compactness-choice-ledger-metric]]; the implications proved without choice in the metric setting are [[thm-compact-implies-the-other-compactness-forms]]. Nothing in that collapse is available here, and the counterexamples of this page are all non-metrizable.
