research/audit/wave7-topology-separation-urysohn.findings.md-130-> For nonempty $S \subseteq X$, $d(\cdot,S)$ is $1$-Lipschitz, hence continuous; $d(x,S)\ge 0$; and $\overline S=\{x:d(x,S)=0\}$ (`lem-distance-to-set-is-lipschitz`; `def-metric-bounded-diameter`; `thm-metric-closure-characterisation`, claim 1). In particular, when $S$ is closed, $d(x,S)=0$ exactly when $x\in S$.
